{
  "requirement": "The `PlainText` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct PlainText;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for PlainText;\nimpl Debug for PlainText;\nimpl Default for PlainText;\nimpl OutlineLang for PlainText;\nimpl Copy for PlainText;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations in `requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.PlainText`**\n1. The public type is `pub struct PlainText;`, a unit struct.\n2. It carries the trait implementations Clone, Debug, Default, OutlineLang and Copy.\n3. Its `OutlineLang` implementation supplies the extension, selection and fingerprint rules. The chapter's refining requirements `requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.items` and `requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.fingerprints` carry the detailed rules.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Declaration and trait implementations:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` generates rustdoc and compares the declaration and trait-implementation set of each specified export. The comparison is exact: `check_declaration` asserts `expected_impls == rustdoc.trait_impls(page)`. A missing or extra Clone, Debug, Default, Copy or OutlineLang implementation would therefore fail it. The test uses `languages::PlainText` as a unit value in other tests, which also shows it is a unit struct.\n- **Extension rule:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` asserts `plain.name() == \"plain-text\"` and `plain.extensions().is_empty()`. `unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors` shows that unclaimed names such as `missing.unclaimed` and `README` fall back to plain text.\n- **Selection rule:** `unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors` checks the following:\n  - the root item has span `0..18`;\n  - blank lines are skipped;\n  - the line items have kind `line`;\n  - the selector is `line@` plus 12 hex digits equal to the hash prefix;\n  - duplicate lines share a selector and distinct lines do not;\n  - `select` resolves a selector to its text;\n  - an empty source gives a single root item.\n- **Fingerprint rule:** `plain_line_fingerprints_use_sha256_words_without_losing_boundaries` asserts a known SHA-256 value for `hello`, whitespace normalization, word boundaries being kept, and the scheme `plain-text-structural-v1:own-v1`. The first test also checks that the structural hash depends on order and joining while the fingerprint does not.\n\n`outline_only_languages_report_unsupported_structural_search` also exercises `PlainText` through `OutlineLang`, but it has no `{test}` reference to this requirement. That test's behavior is not part of this requirement's text, so I did not count it as a marking gap.\n\nI found no obligation of this requirement that the reviewed tests leave untested or unasserted. The detailed rule behaviors are tested and marked on the refining requirements as well as here.",
